{"pageProps":{"note":{"id":"ac09f4a5-496c-49be-9396-2d602537468c","title":"Burtynsky's \"Manufactured Landscapes\" — a counter-example","desc":"Large-format industrial-landscape photography that documents scale beautifully but argues against our restraint rule, filed here as what not to do rather than what to adopt.","updated":1788443359285,"created":1788419688518,"tags":["meta","photography","industrial","counter-example"],"vendor_approved":false,"vendor":"","approved_on":"","custom":{"vendor_approved":false,"vendor":"","approved_on":""},"fname":"sources.photos.burtynsky-manufactured-landscapes","type":"note","vault":{"fsPath":"vault"},"contentHash":"c18b43926409cbc4bbcfc43c21aef0c4","links":[{"type":"frontmatterTag","from":{"fname":"sources.photos.burtynsky-manufactured-landscapes","id":"ac09f4a5-496c-49be-9396-2d602537468c","vaultName":"vault"},"value":"tags.meta","alias":"meta","xvault":false,"to":{"fname":"tags.meta"}},{"type":"frontmatterTag","from":{"fname":"sources.photos.burtynsky-manufactured-landscapes","id":"ac09f4a5-496c-49be-9396-2d602537468c","vaultName":"vault"},"value":"tags.photography","alias":"photography","xvault":false,"to":{"fname":"tags.photography"}},{"type":"frontmatterTag","from":{"fname":"sources.photos.burtynsky-manufactured-landscapes","id":"ac09f4a5-496c-49be-9396-2d602537468c","vaultName":"vault"},"value":"tags.industrial","alias":"industrial","xvault":false,"to":{"fname":"tags.industrial"}},{"type":"frontmatterTag","from":{"fname":"sources.photos.burtynsky-manufactured-landscapes","id":"ac09f4a5-496c-49be-9396-2d602537468c","vaultName":"vault"},"value":"tags.counter-example","alias":"counter-example","xvault":false,"to":{"fname":"tags.counter-example"}}],"anchors":{"the-problem":{"type":"header","text":"The problem","value":"the-problem","line":19,"column":0,"depth":2},"what-they-did":{"type":"header","text":"What they did","value":"what-they-did","line":27,"column":0,"depth":2},"what-we-take":{"type":"header","text":"What we take","value":"what-we-take","line":38,"column":0,"depth":2}},"children":[],"parent":"9fb155f7-93b1-42c9-9ca5-965ead6264cc","data":{}},"body":"<h1 id=\"burtynskys-manufactured-landscapes--a-counter-example\">Burtynsky's \"Manufactured Landscapes\" — a counter-example<a aria-hidden=\"true\" class=\"anchor-heading icon-link\" href=\"#burtynskys-manufactured-landscapes--a-counter-example\"></a></h1>\n<h2 id=\"the-problem\">The problem<a aria-hidden=\"true\" class=\"anchor-heading icon-link\" href=\"#the-problem\"></a></h2>\n<p>Industrial scale is hard to photograph honestly. A quarry, a refinery, or a\nfabrication plant is too large to read from ground level and too abstract\nin a floor plan; photographers who want to convey what \"industrial scale\"\nactually looks like need some way to make magnitude itself legible in a\nsingle frame.</p>\n<h2 id=\"what-they-did\">What they did<a aria-hidden=\"true\" class=\"anchor-heading icon-link\" href=\"#what-they-did\"></a></h2>\n<p>Edward Burtynsky photographs large-scale industrial sites — quarries,\ntailings ponds, refineries, and in China specifically the infrastructure of\nrapid manufacturing growth — using a large-format camera, saturated colour,\nand typically an elevated, panoramic vantage point that lets the whole site\nregister as pattern and scale at once. He has described the work as\nsearching for a tension between attraction and repulsion, and reviewers\nconsistently describe the results as beautiful — the images circulate as\nfine-art prints and museum retrospectives as much as documentary record.</p>\n<h2 id=\"what-we-take\">What we take<a aria-hidden=\"true\" class=\"anchor-heading icon-link\" href=\"#what-we-take\"></a></h2>\n<p>This is worth filing explicitly as a counter-example rather than a\ntechnique to adopt, the way <code>notes.photos</code> already earmarks open-hardware\nphotography as mostly \"what not to do.\" Burtynsky solves our scale problem\n— his elevated vantage points do make magnitude legible — but he solves it\nby making the industrial sublime, which is precisely the \"trust us, don't\nlook\" mystique our own four rules reject, just aimed at factories instead\nof weapons. The panoramic vantage point for conveying scale is transferable;\nthe saturated, art-print treatment is not. If we ever need a wide,\nsite-level shot (a fab floor, a supply chain node) the lesson is to keep\nthat same elevated framing but strip the drama back to something closer to\nour datasheet aesthetic.</p>\n<p>What doesn't transfer: the deliberate beauty is the whole point of\nBurtynsky's project and the opposite of ours; adopting his lighting or\ncolour treatment would undercut the \"legibility beats mystique\" rule this\nwhole page exists to test other sources against.</p>\n<p>Source: [(https://www.edwardburtynsky.com/projects/films/manufactured-landscapes)]</p>\n<hr>\n<h2 id=\"tags\">Tags<a aria-hidden=\"true\" class=\"anchor-heading icon-link\" href=\"#tags\"></a></h2>\n<ol>\n<li><a title=\"Private\" href=\"https://wiki.dendron.so/notes/hfyvYGJZQiUwQaaxQO27q.html\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"private\">meta (Private)</a></li>\n<li><a title=\"Private\" href=\"https://wiki.dendron.so/notes/hfyvYGJZQiUwQaaxQO27q.html\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"private\">photography (Private)</a></li>\n<li><a title=\"Private\" href=\"https://wiki.dendron.so/notes/hfyvYGJZQiUwQaaxQO27q.html\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"private\">industrial (Private)</a></li>\n<li><a title=\"Private\" href=\"https://wiki.dendron.so/notes/hfyvYGJZQiUwQaaxQO27q.html\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"private\">counter-example (Private)</a></li>\n</ol>","noteIndex":{"id":"28a6a50b-4c15-4c7d-b603-5a1d12809f1c","title":"Notes","desc":"Ideas in my own words, revised over time rather than published once.","updated":1788417991064,"created":1788417991064,"tags":["meta"],"custom":{"nav_order":0,"permalink":"/"},"fname":"notes","type":"note","vault":{"fsPath":"vault"},"contentHash":"1684a548ea270e4f1afc2c89cb1e47c9","links":[{"type":"frontm